// The baked-in world: what the browser shows before it can fetch one. It
// stands in for a world that arrives from elsewhere, so it reaches the
// browser exactly as a downloaded one will: it is given the scene's Door,
// reserves ids and sends requests, and nothing else. It never sees a scene
// table, the render system or a GPU handle (the scene module keeps them
// private: the Door is all a sender can hold).
//
// HYDRATE, THEN INJECT. Each object is a description in Cone, ported from
// the example programs of Cone's sculpt and vfx packages (examples are not
// importable, and these are this world's own content, not library code).
// Hydrating one runs its description through the libraries into plain data:
// meshes, materials and their paint images, emitters, and parts naming
// them with their parents and placements (a Hydrated, which holds no id
// and touches no scene). Injecting it defines its meshes and materials
// (one the world shares across objects only once), reserves an id for each
// of its parts and sends that part's Spawn, Place, Parent and Show (or
// Effect) through the Door. The Hydrated is the message: when worlds arrive from another actor,
// that actor hydrates and sends the Hydrated, and only 'inject' runs here.
//
// One object is hydrated and injected a call ('step'), so the browser keeps
// drawing frames while a world arrives, its objects appearing one by one.
//
// THE OBJECTS, in metres in the island's world (y up, +x east, +z south towards
// the sea; the cottage's front wall is centred at (-16, 330) and faces south
// down the path, and the viewer lands on the beach at (-22, 499) facing -z):
//   an amphora, 1.5 m          (a lidded black-figure amphora: its outline traced
//                               from a photograph and lathed, two handles swept,
//                               its bands painted; just east of the path, three
//                               metres before the cottage's steps)
//   a horn-flower, 2 m         (the horn as a plant: its stalk cut short, the
//                               flower's petals on the cut, leaves up it; beside
//                               the amphora)
//   the cottage, 7 m to the ridge (cottage.cone: measured from the reference frame, one
//                               tree of 26 parts: walls, battens, roofs, windows, door,
//                               porch, steps, two wall lanterns, and the brick chimney,
//                               chimney.cone's stack on a brick shaft, flaunching and a
//                               pot, 7.3 m up: bricks in stretcher bond, a colour, normal
//                               and ORM map)
//   a hot-air balloon, 25 m    (sculpt's balloon, the photograph's chevrons, its
//                               envelope painted; one burner head, vfx's burner flame
//                               on it; a wicker basket for two standing riders, open at
//                               the front, a platform they ride on; the launch button,
//                               a red cap on the back rail, whose clicks the world
//                               listens for: they send the balloon on its ride) in the
//                               backyard, 24 m behind the cottage
//   a lathed rook, 0.56 m      (sculpt's lathed rook: one lathe and four merlons joined
//                               on, ivory) on the porch deck's east end, beside the door
//   (the launch button)        (nothing now: the button is in the basket; its place is
//                               the boarding spot, where the lawn route round the
//                               cottage's east end ends)
//   a ball, 1 m across         (checkered; lying on the lawn east of the path, where
//                               a child left it)
//   twelve path lanterns, 0.46 m (cottage.cone: six pairs facing across the path's last 16 m; square, like a solar path light;
//                               post, glass, bulb and head (frame and roof), each a part, in three materials shared with the cottage's wall lanterns)
//   two porch pots, 0.34 m     (porch.cone: a lathed clay pot with a clump of flowers
//                               in it, either side of the door)
//   rocks                      (the rock family, noiserock's meshes in the kit's granite,
//                               scattered by layout.cone: vegetation.cone)
//   the vegetation             (two specimen red maples, the pines and forest maples,
//                               edging stones, hostas, ferns and flowers: one part a copy
//                               of a few variants' meshes; layout.cone says where,
//                               vegetation.cone makes them)
//
// Not in this scene: the chess rook, the horn, the mound and the starship. The
// starship's code (dragonship/, gpu/) stays for a later space scene; hydrateShip
// below is its one way into a world, and nothing calls it.
//
// THE WORLD MOVES. Once a frame, 'tick' reads the world's mail (the button's
// clicks, posted by the browser into the Door) and sends its motions, each
// a formula of the scene's time (motions.cone), as Place and Fire requests.
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the designated file, imports:
//
//   bakedworld.cone   the objects' list and places, hydrate, inject, step, tick
//   motions.cone      the balloon's ride (its path, heading and speed) and its burner's bursts
//   balloon.cone      the balloon and its paint
//   flame.cone        the burner's flame and its pilot light
//   smoke.cone        the chimney's smoke
//   sculptures.cone   the lathed rook, the horn (the horn-flower's stalk)
//   layout.cone       where the vegetation stands: the rules and the seed
//   vegetation.cone   the trees', rocks' and plants' meshes, textures and parts
//   amphora.cone      the amphora, its handles and its paint
//   chimney.cone      the brick chimney (a shaft and a stack) and its maps
//   cottage.cone      the cottage, its materials, and the lanterns
//   lights.cone       what glows and when: dusk and dawn, nearness, pools of light
//   hornflower.cone   the horn-flower
//   porch.cone        the porch's pots and the flowers in them

mod bakedworld;

